  No, it didn't do you any additional good.

>
>It seems to me that before reading a scroll of armor enchantment, it's
>a good idea to shed your suit and put your cloak back on.  You don't
>want to use enchantments on a suit that might be destroyed if you hit a
>polymorph trap.  It seems that everything else just falls off unharmed.
> Comments?

  There are so many aspects to enchanting armor and polytraps 
that I don't know what to say.

  Efficient use of enchant armor scrolls, ditto.

  It's probably better to find a way to be immune to polytraps.

>
>Are there any monsters that can loot a locked chest or box?

  No.  Boxes/chests can be engulfed, but their contents can be
recovered.  Even the engulfing can be protected against.

  Stashing strategy is a big part of the game.  A description
of the "best" ways to do it would be very spoily.

>
>Finally, would anyone like to give me a general plan of action for the
>near future?

  Don't die.  Dead characters rarely accomplish much.  

  Keep carefully trying for better armor.

  Explore carefully, be prepared to run.

  Staying unspoiled will be difficult.

  Make stashes so you can stay unburdened.

  Enjoy the game!



